extends RefCounted
## Fighter kits: what makes each fighter play differently. Per family:
##   archetype   – role shown in the menu (Rushdown, Zoner, Schwergewicht …)
##   weight/speed – override the prompt values (knockback resistance, run speed)
##   standard_name/special_name – names of the two base attacks
##   phys        – movement: jump (m/s), gravity (m/s²), fast_fall (m/s), air (air speed factor),
##                 air_jumps, run (run speed factor), shield (shield size factor), heat (Magmor's gauge)
##   moves       – overrides for the generated moveset (combat.gd build_moveset), one array per move:
##                 [name, dmg, windup, active, recovery, x_min, x_max, y_min, y_max, angle, kb, extras]
##                 dmg/kb are factors of the base attack (standard; specials: the prompt special).
##                 Hitbox x forward / y up from the feet, frames in seconds.
##                 extras: free_angle, all_around, back, rehit, motion_vx/vy, armor (hits below this damage
##                 do not interrupt), shot (projectile spec), blink (instant step, m), intangible,
##                 armor_self / rage_self / counter_time (seconds), use_sig (signature-style mechanic),
##                 super_gain (super meter), repel (reflects shots within radius), clone_swap (swap with
##                 the shadow clone), cooldown, pose.
##   finisher    – own finisher: name, code (F B U D A S), kind (base visuals) and variant (main.gd cinematic)
## Fighters without a kit keep the generated moveset and the default physics.
## The signature special (neutral special) lives in signatures.gd.

